# KNOWN GAP — a BUILTIN METHOD's owned String result, passed STRAIGHT into a
# call argument, is never drop-registered. `todo/t0609` item (2).
#
# THE DISCRIMINATOR IS THE BINDING, AND IT IS ONE LINE:
#     print(x.debug())              -> LEAKS 3 bytes
#     String d = x.debug(); print(d) -> CLEAN
# Binding the result to a named local drop-registers it (`gorget_string_free`
# is emitted); passing it directly into a call does not, so the temp is dropped
# on the floor. Frames: `str_alloc_copy` <- `gorget_string_adopt` <-
# `gorget_int_to_str` <- `main`.
#
# ⚠ THE PRODUCER AXIS IS NARROWER THAN t0609(2)'s HEADLINE, measured here
# rather than assumed. That item frames the class as "a call/await result temp
# consumed as an arg", citing `print(t.await())` and `print(s.speak())`. A
# PLAIN USER FUNCTION returning a heap String in the very same position —
# `print(heavy("alpha", "beta"))` below — is CLEAN at this HEAD. So the
# leaking producers are a SUBSET of "calls", and a fix aimed at every call
# result would be aimed wider than the defect. The clean user-call cell is kept
# in this fixture as a CONTROL precisely so that stays visible.
#
# ⚠ HEAP-FORCED throughout: `x.debug()` and `f.display()` allocate their result
# (3 and 4 bytes), and `heavy` concatenates rather than returning a literal. A
# literal-only version of this program leaks nothing observable and would be a
# false negative (the lesson `todo/t0705` was filed for).
#
# ⚠ ONLY LeakSanitizer CAN SEE THIS. stdout is correct today, so this is wired
# to `assert_gg_sanitize_clean` (`detect_leaks=1`), never to `run_gg`.
#
# ⚠ t0609(2) warns the fix must be CONDITIONAL: the same result also binds to a
# VarDecl in the control cells below, and drop-registering it unconditionally
# double-frees those. This fixture holds both cells for that reason.
#
# Un-ignore + promote out of `known_gaps/` when the temp is dropped.

String heavy(String a, String b):
    return a + b

int main():
    int x = 21
    float f = 7.5

    # CONTROL — a user call's result temp at a call-arg position. CLEAN today.
    print(heavy("alpha", "beta"))

    # THE GAP — a builtin method's result temp at the same position. LEAKS.
    print(x.debug())
    print(f.display())

    # CONTROL — the same producers, bound to a named local first. CLEAN today,
    # and what a fix must not turn into a double free.
    String bound = heavy("gamma", "delta")
    print(bound)
    String d = x.debug()
    print(d)
    return 0
